# ACOS Operating Spine v1.2 — Remediation Ledger

**Phase 2.3. Issued 2026-09-03. Sole authoritative record of the disposition of every BLOCKING defect raised by the second independent red team.**

Source: `57-second-redteam-remediation.md`, which is the authoritative remediation specification. Verdict source: `52-second-redteam-executive-verdict.md` (CONDITIONAL PASS — REMEDIATION REQUIRED, 0 FATAL · 22 BLOCKING · 24 MATERIAL · 6 MINOR · 4 WORDING · 10 attacks defeated). Gate source: `58-implementation-gate.md`.

**Twenty-two entries. No merges. No silent consolidation.** Every entry terminates in exactly one of `APPLIED`, `APPLIED WITH EXPLICIT RESIDUAL`, `NOT APPLIED — BLOCKING`.

---

## 0. Scope correction, recorded before the ledger

`57 §0`'s prose header states that third review is required for *"SR-A1 and SR-B2"*. **`SR-B2` does not exist.** `57`'s own tier table, its `§6`, `52 §4` and `58 §9` all agree that the third-review items are `SR-A1`, `SR-A2` (jointly, one mechanism) and `SR-S2`. This ledger records the typo and does not propagate it. **No `SR-B2` finding is created anywhere in the v1.2 package.**

Two design additions require third review, represented by three finding ids:

| Review mechanism | Finding ids | Why it is a new mechanism |
|---|---|---|
| **A — audit independent input + degraded-mode corroboration** | SR-A1, SR-A2 | Changes what the audit plane *is*: it acquires an independent input signal and a veto over a dispatch relaxation |
| **B — standing exposure cessation and release** | SR-S2 | Introduces a lifecycle whose release condition has a commercial cost that must be visible before it is built |

