## 2. The ledger

### SR-C1 — `I18`'s equality is ill-typed

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | CAN-01 (`53 §1`), traced in `54 §3.1` |
| **Defect** | `I18` requires `dispatch_payload.monetary_effect == authorisation.exposure == reservation.amount` while `26 §2.1` defines exposure to include `cost_components[]`. Vacuous if `monetary_effect` is a copy of the kernel figure; false for every correctly constructed refund if it is the dispatched amount; and for `fulfilment.reship` the first term has no referent because the vendor request carries no money field. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `26 §2.1`, `26 §2.2` row 12, `26 §8`, `24 §3` K4, `36 §2`, `51 §3.1`/`§5`, invariant registry |
| **Required change** | Split `exposure.monetary_amount` into `vendor_amount` (nullable) and `total_exposure`. Restate `I18` as separate type-correct assertions. Refund policy must test `total_exposure` against the cap. Declare a per-action-class settlement tolerance. |
| **Applied change** | `26 §2.1` v1.2 carries the nine-field `exposure` block of `57 §1`. `I18` is now a conjunction of four lettered clauses **I18a–I18d** (`§3` of the registry). `26 §8`'s refund policy tests `context.exposure.total_exposure <= 25.00`. `51 §5.1` v1.2 declares `settlement_tolerance` per class with two kinds — `EXACT` for classes whose settled cost is fully determined pre-dispatch, `BAND(basis)` for `[ESTIMATE]`-graded classes — and `MIE_cost` acquires a p50/p95 band so the band has a declared basis. |
| **Invariant** | `I18` restated as I18a (`dispatch_payload.monetary_effect == exposure.vendor_amount` where a vendor monetary field exists), I18b (`reservation.amount == exposure.total_exposure`, always), I18c (`total_exposure >= vendor_amount` where `vendor_amount` is non-null, equality only for classes declaring no cost components), I18d (settled cost within the class's declared `settlement_tolerance` against `total_exposure`). `I3`'s reservation term now unambiguously references `total_exposure`. |
| **Test** | `36 §2.1` VC-C1: per-class construction fixture with a hand-computed table, containing at least one null-`vendor_amount` class (`fulfilment.reship`) and one non-zero-cost-component class (`refund.create`). Fixture authored from the processor's published fee schedule, never from the production constructor. |
| **Third review** | No |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED WITH EXPLICIT RESIDUAL** |
| **Residual** | `unit_cost_p95` for `fulfilment.reship` and `order.address.edit` is `[ESTIMATE]`-graded and **unmeasured**. Marked `IMPLEMENTATION_VALIDATION_REQUIRED` in `51 §3.3`. Conservative default: the interim p95 is the figure the owner signs, and a class whose p95 is unmeasured is autonomy-eligible only within that interim value. `58 §12` item 12 remains the only unforgeable test. |
| **Sections changed** | `26 §2.1`, `26 §2.2`, `26 §8`, `26 §10.1`, `24 §3` K4, `30 §5.3`, `36 §2`, `51 §3.1`, `51 §3.3`, `51 §5` |

