### SR-C3 — positional selector permits substitution

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | CAN-03 (`53 §1`) — the constructed path in which the executed effect is economically different from the selected one and `I18`, `I21`, `I2`, `I3`, `I29`, `I31` all hold |
| **Defect** | Index *n* denotes a different effect at C′ than at selection time when enumeration membership changes. `SELECTOR_INVALID` fires only when the set shrinks past the index — the benign case. Reordering is undetectable by an ordinal. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `26 §2.0`, `26 §2.1`, `26 §7` step C′, `24 §3` K4, `36 §2` |
| **Required change** | Content-address the options. `option_id = H(action_class ‖ resource_id ‖ semantic_option_digest)`. `ProposedIntent.selector` becomes `{enumeration_id, option_id}`. C′ re-enumerates under the lock and denies rather than substituting. |
| **Applied change** | `26 §2.0` v1.2 replaces the index with `selector { enumeration_id, option_id }`. `26 §7` step C′ v1.2 re-enumerates under the entity advisory lock and denies `SELECTOR_STALE` when `option_id` is absent from the live set, `SELECTOR_ENUMERATION_STALE` when `enumeration_id.computed_at` exceeds the class's `max_age`, and `SELECTOR_MALFORMED` when the pair does not parse. **Substitution is never performed.** `selector` remains one field for `I21`'s purposes. `26 §2.2` gains the `semantic_option_digest` definition per class. |
| **Invariant** | `I21` unchanged in content (`selector` is still one of the four permitted fields). New **I53**: no effect is dispatched whose `option_id` was absent from the enumeration computed under the C′ lock. Enforcement RUNTIME at C′ + DB (the `option_id` is a not-null column on the effect row and is re-derivable from the journaled enumeration). |
| **Test** | `36 §2.3` VC-C3: `53 §1` CAN-03's reordering scenario with an injected concurrent partial refund, asserting `SELECTOR_STALE`. **Mandatory negative control**: the same test with positional selectors must produce the substitution, or the test does not detect the bug. |
| **Third review** | No |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED** |
| **Sections changed** | `26 §2.0`, `26 §2.1`, `26 §2.2`, `26 §7`, `24 §3` K4, `36 §2`, `35 §12.4` |

