### SR-C4 — `constructor_version` unrecorded

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | CAN-04 (`53 §1`), RES-06 (`53 §5`) |
| **Defect** | `26 §11`'s reproducibility claim is false across any constructor change, and `I18`'s settlement-side investigation cannot identify which constructor computed the disputed exposure. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `26 §2.1`, `26 §11`, `26 §12`, `24 §3` K3/K4, `30 §5`, `50` |
| **Required change** | `constructor_version` on `AuthorizationRequest`, `AuthorizationDecision`, the journal row and the approval binding. Constructors become signed control artifacts. Declare semantic versus non-semantic change classes, consumed by SR-R1's resume rule. |
| **Applied change** | `constructor_version` is a not-null field in all four locations and in the replay context. `50 §2` gains **class 19 — Effect constructors** (owner signature, second factor, halt scope = the constructor's action class). A `ConstructorVersionRecord{constructor_id, version, semantic_major, non_semantic_minor, changed_fields[], semantic_change: bool, signed_at}` is a signed artifact; **a bump that changes any of exposure computation, enumeration membership, `semantic_option_digest`, counterparty derivation, `value_direction`, recoverability or the dispatch payload field set is semantic by definition** and cannot be declared non-semantic. `26 §11` v1.2 restates reproducibility as *"same inputs, same `policy_version`, same `constructor_version`, same verdict"*. Replay under a different semantic version is **refused**, not silently recomputed. |
| **Invariant** | `I19` extended to constructors as a control-artifact class. New **I61**: every `AuthorizationRequest`, `AuthorizationDecision`, journal row and approval binding records a `constructor_version` resolving to a signed `ConstructorVersionRecord`; no approval resumes under a constructor whose `semantic_major` differs from the bound one. |
| **Test** | `36 §2.4` VC-C4: replay a recorded decision under a bumped semantic version and assert refusal rather than a silently different result; replay under a non-semantic bump and assert the replay succeeds and reproduces the recorded verdict. |
| **Third review** | No |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED** |
| **Sections changed** | `26 §2.1`, `26 §7`, `26 §11`, `26 §12`, `24 §3` K3, `24 §3` K4, `24 §3` K9, `30 §5.3`, `50 §2`, `36 §2` |

