### SR-S1 — rolling-window forward exposure undefined

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | STD-01 (`53 §2`), `54 §2.4` |
| **Defect** | Four of `51 §2`'s nine windows are rolling 24h. A rolling window has no end to integrate to and no boundary at which to re-reserve, so `Standing(day) = $6.00` does not follow from the declared semantics and R2's pause mechanism has no trigger point. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `51 §2`, `24 §3` K5, `26 §4`, `26 §7` step R, `26 §10.1` |
| **Required change** | `boundary_kind ∈ {DISCRETE, ROLLING}` as a declared window column. `standing.required` grants may reference DISCRETE windows only; referencing a rolling window is a catalogue defect and denies. Redeclare `W_DAY_ADSPEND` as a calendar day on the company timezone, evaluated on the database clock. |
| **Applied change** | `51 §2` v1.2 declares `boundary_kind` on every window. **All nine production windows are DISCRETE** — calendar day or calendar month, company timezone, database clock. `ROLLING` remains in the type with its method defined in `51 §2.1` (trailing-interval balance, continuous ageing) and is marked **`NOT_ADMISSIBLE_AT_MVP`** with a stated reason: a rolling balance cannot be expressed as a single `CHECK`-constrained `window_balance` row at a single commit point, which is `I3`'s enforcement mechanism (LIM-05). A calendar-boundary algorithm is therefore **not** reused for a rolling interval — no rolling interval remains. `26 §4` denies at catalogue validation on a `standing.required` grant referencing a ROLLING window. |
| **Invariant** | `I3` v1.2 states that standing forward exposure is defined only against DISCRETE windows. `I23`'s test acquires a boundary to test at. |
| **Test** | `36 §2.5` VC-S1: a rate grant referencing a ROLLING window must deny at catalogue validation; boundary re-reservation at a calendar-day boundary with expiry inside the window, asserting pause. |
| **Third review** | No |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED** |
| **Sections changed** | `51 §2`, `51 §2.1`, `24 §3` K5, `26 §4`, `26 §7`, `26 §10.1`, `50 §2` |

