### SR-S2 — standing headroom release condition unspecified

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | STD-02 (`53 §2`), `54 §4.2` Path B |
| **Defect** | On a pause whose outcome is unknown, releasing forward exposure returns headroom while the platform continues spending — the v1.0 defect R2 exists to close, reached through the pause path — and a successor authorisation's `reconciler_match_rule` then absorbs the predecessor's charges so `I22` stays silent. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `24 §3` K5, `26 §10.1`, `30 §5.1`, `35 §7`, `51 §3.2`, invariant registry |
| **Required change** | `PAUSE_PENDING` in the status enum; forward exposure retained in `LIVE` and `PAUSE_PENDING`, released only on `REVOKED`; `REVOKED` requires a verification read showing zero incremental platform spend across a per-adapter `cessation_lag`; `I3` gains the retained term; `reconciler_match_rule` scoped to one `standing_authorization_id`. |
| **Applied change** | `24 §3` K5 v1.2 declares the five-state machine `LIVE | PAUSE_PENDING | PAUSED | EXPIRED | REVOKED` with the full transition table in `24 §3.1`. **Forward exposure is retained in every non-`REVOKED` status** — this is stronger than `57`'s two-status retention and is recorded as a deliberate strengthening, not a substitution. `PAUSED` is a display state meaning *the vendor acknowledged the pause*; it is **not** a release state. `REVOKED` requires `I54`'s cessation verification. `cessation_lag` is an adapter characteristic with a provenance field. `reconciler_match_rule` is a bounded predicate scoped to a single `standing_authorization_id` (`51 §3.2`), so a successor cannot absorb a predecessor's charges. |
| **Invariant** | `I3` extended (term 2 is now *all non-`REVOKED` standing forward exposure*). `I22` narrowed to a per-authorisation match. New **I54**: no `StandingAuthorization` transitions to `REVOKED` without a verification read showing zero incremental spend attributable to that `standing_authorization_id` across `cessation_lag`. |
| **Test** | `36 §2.6` VC-S2a/b/c: pause dispatch → adapter timeout → assert forward exposure retained, status `PAUSE_PENDING`, second `campaign.budget.set` denied `WINDOW_EXHAUSTED`. Verification read showing continued spend → assert an `I22` incident **against the original authorisation**. `cessation_lag` measurement is an S3 obligation. |
| **Third review** | **YES — Review Mechanism B** |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED WITH EXPLICIT RESIDUAL** |
| **Residual** | `cessation_lag` for Google Ads and Meta is **`UNMEASURED`**. Vendor documentation does not state how long after a pause the platform's spend reporting settles (`58 §12` item 9). **Conservative default when `UNMEASURED`: no `REVOKED` transition is available at all.** Forward exposure is held until the last referenced window closes, at which point it lapses with the window. Commercial consequence stated in `51 §3.2` and `26 §10.5`: **pause-and-reauthorise within one window is not possible**, and until `cessation_lag` is measured, advertising is effectively a whole-window commitment. This is `58 §13` condition 3's trigger and it is a business-model finding if the measurement comes back long. |
| **Sections changed** | `24 §3` K5, `24 §3.1` (new), `26 §7`, `26 §10.1`, `26 §10.5` (new), `30 §5.1`, `35 §7`, `51 §3.2`, `36 §2` |

---

### SR-S3 — expiry/revocation deadlock

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | STD-03 (`53 §2`) |
| **Defect** | `expires_at` mirrors grant expiry; the revocation effect requires a matching grant at step I; the grant has expired; `DENY: NO_GRANT`; the authorisation cannot pause and spend continues. `I23` is defeated by the mechanism enforcing it. And `24 §3` K4 accepts a kernel-originated request that `26 §7` has no branch for. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `24 §3` K4, `24 §3` K5, `26 §4`, `26 §7`, `51 §3.2` |
| **Required change** | A kernel-created standing revocation authority scoped to one class, one resource, one `standing_authorization_id`, zero monetary exposure, `expires_at = grant.expires_at + cessation_grace`. Plus an explicit `KERNEL_SERVICE` branch in `26 §7` naming exactly which steps it skips and which it must not. |
| **Applied change** | `24 §3` K5 v1.2 declares `StandingRevocationAuthority` as kernel-created state, created atomically with the `StandingAuthorization` in the authorising transaction, and destroyed only when the authorisation reaches `REVOKED`. `26 §7.1` v1.2 is a new subsection specifying the `KERNEL_SERVICE` branch: **skipped** — step I (grant match), step L (evidence requirements), step N (autonomy ledger), step K (counterparty novelty, because the resource is fixed at creation); **never skipped** — step B (schema), C (catalogue), C2/C′ (constructor and canonicalisation), D (principal), E (categorical prohibitions), F (platform status/kill switch), G/H/H′/H″ (preconditions, grade, contradiction, delegation), M (per-action max, read from the revocation authority's own declared bound of zero monetary), R (reservation, which is a zero-amount reservation row and still a row), S (approval requirement, which is `NONE` for this authority by construction), T–V (idempotency), W (signed decision), X (audit write). The authority can authorise nothing else: its `resource_selector` is an equality on one `resource_ref` and its `action_class_selector` is a singleton. |
| **Invariant** | `I23` becomes achievable. New **I55**: every `StandingAuthorization` in a non-`REVOKED` status has a live `StandingRevocationAuthority` whose `expires_at` exceeds the authorisation's own by at least `cessation_grace`. |
| **Test** | `36 §2.7` VC-S3: expire the advertising grant with a live standing authorisation and assert the pause dispatches; assert the standing revocation authority cannot authorise any other class, any other resource, or any monetary amount; assert a `KERNEL_SERVICE` request that names a prohibited class still denies `PROHIBITED`. |
| **Third review** | No |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED** |
| **Sections changed** | `24 §3` K4, `24 §3` K5, `26 §4`, `26 §7`, `26 §7.1` (new), `29 §3`, `49 §3`, `51 §3.2` |

