### SR-L2 — window ceilings undeclared

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | LIM-02 (`53 §4`), LIM-05, STD-07, LIM-07 |
| **Defect** | `I3` reads `window ceiling` and no artifact declares one. Ceiling-as-sum-over-grants makes `I3` vacuous; independently declared ceiling makes `MAL_monetary` over-count when grants share a window; and `51`'s fixture cannot distinguish them because six of nine windows have one referencing grant. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `51 §2`, `26 §4`, `26 §10.1`, `24 §3` K5, registry `I3`, `I7` |
| **Required change** | Windows declare `max_monetary`, `max_count`, `max_irrecoverable_units`. **Grants may only narrow, never widen.** `MAL_monetary(w)` becomes `min(window.max_monetary, Σ grant-derived terms)`. Resolve the heterogeneous MIE count units. |
| **Applied change** | `51 §2` v1.2 declares all three ceilings on all nine windows plus the two override windows. `26 §4` v1.2 states the narrowing rule precisely, because the imprecision is what made LIM-02 ambiguous: **each individual grant's derived term must be ≤ the window's ceiling (a grant may only narrow); the *sum* over grants referencing a window may exceed the ceiling, and the ceiling binds.** That is the distinction between the two repairs LIM-02 identified, and it selects the second — the window is the binding object and `I3` is not vacuous. `26 §10.1` v1.2: `MAL_monetary(w) = min(window.max_monetary, Σ_g min(window.max_monetary, g.per_action_max.monetary × g.window(w).max_count))`. `24 §3` K5 v1.2 declares the enforcement mechanism `window_balance(company_id, window_id, reserved, standing, presumed_settled, realised, ceiling_monetary, ceiling_count, ceiling_irrecoverable)` with a `CHECK` taken `FOR UPDATE`, which replaces the registry's incorrect "exclusion constraint" claim (LIM-05, applied here because `I3` is otherwise unimplementable). `W_DAY_MIE`/`W_MONTH_MIE`'s heterogeneous counts are resolved by **declared per-class sub-ceilings within the named window** (`max_count_by_class{}`), not by leaving it implicit. |
| **Invariant** | `I3` becomes evaluable and its enforcement column is corrected to the mechanism that can express a sum bound. `I7` gains the window cap as a term. |
| **Test** | `36 §2.10` VC-L2: fixture F2's two grants of different classes on one window with a binding window cap — assert the second denies `WINDOW_EXHAUSTED` before its own grant count is reached, and assert `MAL_monetary` displays the **window cap**, not the grant sum. Plus F2's two same-class grants on one window (STD-07) and two standing authorisations on one window. |
| **Third review** | No |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED** |
| **Sections changed** | `26 §4`, `26 §10.1`, `26 §10.3`, `24 §3` K5, `51 §2`, `51 §7` (new), `36 §2`, `50 §2` |

