### SR-R1 — reservation vs OWNER approval lifetime

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | RES-01 (`53 §5`), RES-05, RES-06, RES-09, `56 §1.2`–`§1.4` |
| **Defect** | `26 §12` gives OWNER approvals no expiry; `24 §3` K5 reaps reservations. The reservation is guaranteed to be reaped before an OWNER approval arrives, and R′ covers *insufficient*, not *absent*. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `26 §12`, `26 §7`, `24 §3` K5, `24 §3` K9, `25 §12` |
| **Required change** | Reservation TTL derives from the approval tier's SLA; OWNER-tier reservations exempt from reaping and attributed to `I32`. R′ gains an explicit `RESERVATION_ABSENT` denial. A bounded next state after any verify-mode denial: `RemedyObligation` plus an auto-enqueued fresh proposal at the same tier. Semantic comparison on constructor bump. |
| **Applied change** | `26 §12` v1.2 declares `reservation_ttl = approval_tier.sla + reaper_grace` — TIER_1 24h + 6h, TIER_2 48h + 6h — and **OWNER-tier reservations are exempt from reaping**, with their held exposure attributed to `I32`'s starvation metric so the cost of an unattended approval is visible rather than silent. `24 §3` K9 v1.2 declares the explicit **Approval state machine** the mission requires: `PENDING | APPROVED | RESUMING | CONSUMED | DENIED | EXPIRED | SUPERSEDED`, with the legal transitions tabulated and a unique partial constraint on `(approval_id)` in `RESUMING`, so a second concurrent resume cannot start — closing the gap that `I42` only caught at step T, after R′ and after the state transition. `26 §7` step R′ v1.2: an absent, released or expired `reservation_id` denies **`RESERVATION_ABSENT`** and emits a `RemedyObligation` (see SR-R1's Part 13 companion below). On resume under a newer constructor, comparison is **semantic**: unchanged `total_exposure` plus a payload differing only in fields the `ConstructorVersionRecord` declares non-semantic resumes; anything else denies `CONSTRUCTOR_SEMANTIC_CHANGE` and re-proposes. |
| **Invariant** | New **I58**: no denied verify-mode resume for a class carrying an unmet obligation exists without a linked `RemedyObligation`. New **I60**: every `Approval` transition is in the declared transition set, and no `Approval` has more than one `RESUMING` entry. |
| **Test** | `36 §2.13` VC-R1a/b/c: approve after the TIER_1 reservation TTL and assert `RESERVATION_ABSENT` plus an obligation record; deploy a constructor bump mid-queue and assert semantically-equivalent approvals resume while others re-propose; attempt two concurrent resumes on one `(approval_id, key)` and assert the second is refused **before** R′. |
| **Third review** | No |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED** |
| **Sections changed** | `24 §3` K5, `24 §3` K9, `25 §12`, `26 §7`, `26 §12`, `36 §2` |

