### SR-R2 — hand proof incomplete

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | RES-02 (`53 §5`), `56 §3.1`, `56 §3.3` |
| **Defect** | `26 §11.2` covers eleven of nineteen authority-bearing classes and omits `goodwill.credit.issue` and `order.address.edit`, both granted in `51 §3`, plus `campaign.pause`, `webhook.subscription.*`, reconciler resolution, `entitlement.issue/revoke` and `supplier.relationship.create`. It is the only proof of P4 until symcc returns. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `26 §11`, `26 §11.2`, `37 §7`, `36 §3` |
| **Required change** | Complete the table over all authority-bearing classes with four columns: `value_direction`, reachable `counterparty.novelty`, reachable `customer_novelty`, and P4/P4a/P6/P7 status. **Include P6 reachability.** Any class whose direction is not expressible is a finding, not a blank. |
| **Applied change** | `26 §11.2` v1.2 is a complete table over the **twenty-two** authority-bearing classes in the v1.2 catalogue (nineteen from `56 §3.1` plus `price.change`, `social.post` and `platform.message.send`, which `26 §5` assigns recoverability to and which therefore carry authority), with six columns: `value_direction`, reachable `counterparty.novelty`, reachable `customer_novelty`, P4, P4a/P7, and **P6 reachability**. Five classes are recorded as **EXCLUDED FROM AUTONOMOUS MVP EXECUTION** rather than squeezed into the taxonomy — split-tender refunds, cross-currency monetary classes, `email.campaign.send`, chargeback acceptance and any class with no registered constructor — each with the reason and the disqualifier. `26 §11.3` v1.2 works the difficult examples the mission names: goodwill/store credit, gift-card value, split tender, marketplace settlement, third-party beneficiary, subscription credit, affiliate payout, chargeback acceptance. |
| **Invariant** | None new; P4's interim evidence becomes complete. A CI check asserts one row per catalogue class, so a new class cannot be added without a row — the generate-and-diff discipline `I14` applies to capability declarations, applied here. |
| **Test** | `36 §3.2` VC-R2: the table is the artifact; the CI check is the test. Plus a construction test per class asserting the computed `counterparty.id` and `novelty` against a hand-authored fixture **including the stale-allowlist case** — the test `56 §3.2` says is named nowhere. |
| **Third review** | No, provided the completed table contains no class whose direction requires an extension beyond SR-R3's six values. **Verified: it does not.** |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED** |
| **Sections changed** | `26 §5`, `26 §11`, `26 §11.2`, `26 §11.3` (new), `36 §3`, `37 §7`, `51 §3` |

