### SR-R3 — `settlement_direction` incomplete

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Source attack** | RES-03 (`53 §5`), RES-07, RES-10, CAN-07, `56 §2.1` |
| **Defect** | `goodwill.credit.issue` — a monetary class entering `MAL_monetary`, granted in the fixture — is neither outbound to a counterparty nor inbound to the original instrument. The same gap covers the gift-card portion of a split-tender refund, a remedy to a gift recipient, and goods redirection. |
| **Affected artifacts** | `26 §2.1`, `26 §8`, `26 §11`, `24 §3` K4, `50 §2` class 3, `51 §3.1` |
| **Required change** | Rename `settlement_direction` to `value_direction` and extend to six values. Restate P4 as *"no policy path permits a NOVEL destination for any class whose `value_direction` is outbound"*. `INTERNAL_LIABILITY` governed by caps plus a redemption bound, no novelty test. Make refund `instrument` an enumerated dimension. |
| **Applied change** | `value_direction` replaces `settlement_direction` throughout, with six values: `NONE`, `INBOUND_ORIGINAL_INSTRUMENT`, `OUTBOUND_TO_COUNTERPARTY`, `INTERNAL_LIABILITY`, `OUTBOUND_TO_THIRD_PARTY_BENEFICIARY`, `OUTBOUND_GOODS_TO_ADDRESS`. P4 v1.2: *"For every action class whose `value_direction` is outbound — `OUTBOUND_TO_COUNTERPARTY`, `OUTBOUND_TO_THIRD_PARTY_BENEFICIARY` or `OUTBOUND_GOODS_TO_ADDRESS` — no policy path permits a NOVEL destination."* One property, both BEC shapes, money and goods. `INTERNAL_LIABILITY` is governed by per-action and window caps **plus a declared redemption bound** (`51 §3.1`: outstanding store-credit liability ≤ `$200.00`, entering `MAL_monetary` as its own window `W_LIABILITY_OUTSTANDING`) and carries no novelty test because there is no external destination. Refund `instrument` becomes an **enumerated dimension**: the refund enumeration is two-dimensional over `(line, parent_transaction)` with SR-C3's `option_id`, so `26 §8`'s `instrument == "original"` tests an enumerated property rather than a constructor assertion, and split-tender orders become *expressible* — and are nonetheless **excluded from autonomous MVP execution** per `58 §11`. `26 §11.4` v1.2 adds the per-adapter enforceability table RES-10 requires: for each monetary class and each adapter, is the destination processor-derived (structural) or payload-selectable (policy-only)? |
| **Invariant** | P4 restated; P4a unchanged in content, with chargeback acceptance removed from its enumeration because no governed class exists (LIM-08). New **I59**: no class in the catalogue has a null `value_direction`. |
| **Test** | `36 §3.3` VC-R3a/b/c: assert every catalogue class has a non-null direction; assert a split-tender refund enumerates per `(line, parent_transaction)` and then denies `NOT_CANONICALISABLE` at MVP; assert a gift-card destination held by a third party is classified `OUTBOUND_TO_THIRD_PARTY_BENEFICIARY` and that NOVEL denies. |
| **Third review** | No |
| **Disposition** | **APPLIED** |
| **Sections changed** | `26 §2.1`, `26 §5`, `26 §8`, `26 §11`, `26 §11.2`, `26 §11.3` (new), `26 §11.4` (new), `24 §3` K4, `50 §2`, `51 §3.1` |

