## 4. `57 §7` compliance check — did any remediation weaken an invariant?

`57 §7` and `58 §13` condition 1 make this the reconsideration trigger for the whole verdict. Checked item by item, in the four places `57` names specifically.

| `57 §7` prohibition | v1.2 state | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| *"`I18` must not be relaxed to a tolerance that admits omitted cost components"* | `I18b` is an **exact equality** — `reservation.amount == exposure.total_exposure` — with no tolerance at all. The tolerance is on `I18d`, the **settlement** leg, where it is per-class, declared, and `EXACT` for every class whose settled cost is fully determined pre-dispatch. An omitted cost component fails `I18b` at construction, before any tolerance is reached. `I12` forbids widening a band within 30 days of a discrepancy it would resolve. | **Not weakened** |
| *"`I17` must not be restated as one-sided and called complete"* | `I17` is restated as **transport completeness** and explicitly labelled as such in `30 §5`, the registry, `36 §1` and `22 §3.1`. The unqualified claim is relocated to `I8` with its coverage limits attached at every citation. The restatement is a **narrowing of the claim to what the mechanism establishes**, plus a **new mechanism** (`I17e`'s attestation) that closes tail truncation. | **Not weakened** |
| *"`I3` must not drop the `PRESUMED_SETTLED` term because it is inconvenient"* | `I3` v1.2 has four terms including `PRESUMED_SETTLED`, and the term persists until settlement resolves it. The headroom the owner needs comes from a signed override window that enters `MAL_total`. | **Not weakened — term added** |
| *"P4 must not be narrowed further to make the hand proof shorter"* | P4 is **broadened**, from one outbound direction to three, covering goods as well as money. The hand proof grew from eleven rows to twenty-two plus five explicit exclusions, and gained a P6 reachability column it did not have. | **Not weakened — broadened** |

**Additional self-check, because the pattern `52 §3` names is a missing quantity rather than a weakened invariant.** Every quantity in `52 §3`'s table of nine now has a declared home:

| `52 §3` missing quantity | Declared in v1.2 |
|---|---|
| Window monetary ceilings | `51 §2` — all eleven windows, `Money | UNBOUNDED`, not nullable |
| `min(absent, x)` convention | `26 §10.1` — typed rule; `null` is a schema violation |
| Per-class `I18` settlement tolerance | `51 §5.1` — `EXACT` or `BAND(basis)` per class, in the action catalogue |
| Order-driven per-order rate limit | `51 §3.4` — 1, second fulfilment requires TIER_2 |
| Order-driven ratio anomaly threshold | `51 §3.4` — 1.05 over trailing 7 days, `min_denominator = 20` |
| Standing headroom release condition | `24 §3.1` — `REVOKED` only, after `I54`'s cessation verification |
| Overdelivery allowance in forward exposure | `51 §3.2` — `daily_overdelivery_multiplier = 2.0`, `monthly_basis_multiplier = 30.4`, both DOCUMENTED and cited |
| `reconciler_match_rule` specificity | `51 §3.2` — bounded predicate scoped to one `standing_authorization_id` |
| Journal row canonicalisation | `30 §5.3` — `ACOS-JCS-1`, defined once, control artifact class 20 |

