## 5. Ledger verdict

**Twenty-two of twenty-two BLOCKING findings are `APPLIED` or `APPLIED WITH EXPLICIT RESIDUAL`. Zero remain `NOT APPLIED — BLOCKING`.**

Every residual is a quantity that architecture reasoning cannot settle, each carrying an `IMPLEMENTATION_VALIDATION_REQUIRED` marker, a conservative default that fails closed, and a named slice in `58 §12` at which it is measured. No residual is a deferred decision dressed as an unknown.

**This ledger authorises nothing.** `58`'s implementation gate remains closed; see `phase2-v1.2-changelog.md §9`.
